ISSUE TITLE: security: Cargo.lock v4 format silently ignored by parser
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
## Problem

The `parse_cargo_lock()` function in `src/cargo_lock.rs` only handles `version = 3` format. Cargo.lock v4 (introduced in Rust 1.78) has `version = 4` and is now the default for new projects.

When a v4 lockfile is parsed, all packages silently appear to have empty dependency lists, causing:
- False negatives for typosquat/inventory attacks
- Missing native dependency surface detection
- No error or warning to the user

## Evidence

Tests in `tests/` only include v3 fixtures. The parser's version match is:
```rust
if version != 3 { /* skip */ }
```

## Proposal

1. Add support for Cargo.lock v4 format (the `version = 4` line)
2. v4 format is mostly identical to v3 but may have additional fields
3. Warn (not error) on unknown versions
4. Add v4 test fixtures from real-world projects
5. Document supported versions in README

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Cargo.lock v4 parsed correctly
- [ ] v3 fixtures still parse correctly (backward compat)
- [ ] Unknown version produces a warning to stderr
- [ ] Tests with v4 lockfile pass
- [ ] README documents supported versions

